{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T17:00:39.550Z","ordinal":1677,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a06d5d-80fe-78b3-934b-c7369e14e25c","call_id":"call_IjxJab4blX57PQVPFmw4BO7t","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Community | OpenAI Developers (https://developers.openai.com/community)\nciteturn28search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; See programs Share what you built Submit your project, demo, or workflow to the OpenAI developer showcase. ... Codex Ambassadors Host local workshops and meetups for developers in your city. ... > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to codex cloud (with 2 attempts) > got back to my computer, compared both attempts, picked the better one, synced it back to my computer > continued to iterate on it locally ... Codex 5.3 xhigh spark has been phenomenal - you’re able to stay in a state of flow building.\n\n### Victor Mota\n\n@vimota\n\nOpenAI got me with the 2x increased usage limits on the Codex desktop app. It's a really nice experience. Super smooth - claude code app is so laggy. And the handoff experience is amazing. > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to codex cloud (with 2 attempts) > got back to my computer, compared both attempts, picked the better one, synced it back to my computer > continued to iterate on it locally\n\nMar 13, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Derya Unutmaz, MD\n\n@DeryaTR_\n\nMy new Sunday morning routine: 1. Get coffee 2. Check GPT-5.4 projects on the Codex App, continue & start new ones 4. Launch ChatGPT 5.4 Pro for fresh brainstorming sessions 5. Think/learn how to use the 90% of AI capabilities I have yet to explore 6. Drink more coffee\n\nMar 8, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Evan You\n\n@youyuxi\n\nDid a full repo internal / public docs vs. source code alignment check + update - GPT 5.4 did a significantly better job than Opus 4.6. Note this is not a coding task but more like research / documentation. Same prompt but GPT 5.4's proposed revisions captured my intent much...\n\nMar 8, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### ashe\n\n@ashebytes\n\ngiven the interest, I productized my video hub! - have 1 place for video drafts + X, Youtube, tiktok vids - use the studio to comment + collab with others - get transcripts + add API keys for autosyncs/agent chat made with codex 5.3 🖤 linked below\n\nMar 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### John Jung\n\n@johnjjung\n\nCodex 5.3 xhigh spark has been phenomenal - you’re able to stay in a state of flow building. The focus and power of hitting problem after problem is incredible.\n\nMar 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### David Marcus\n\n@davidmarcus\n\nIt's wild that every time you run a Codex code review from Claude Code, it finds critical issues. Not 95% of the times, 100%.\n\nMar 28, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Garry Tan\n\n@garrytan\n\nOK Codex is GOAT at finding bugs and finding plan errors\n\nMar 19, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Victor Mota\n\n@vimota\n\nOpenAI got me with the 2x increased usage limits on the Codex desktop app. It's a really nice experience. Super smooth - claude code app is so laggy. And the handoff experience is amazing. > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to codex cloud (with 2 attempts) > got back to my computer, compared both attempts, picked the better one, synced it back to my computer > continued to iterate on it locally\n\nMar 13, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### ashe\n\n@ashebytes\n\ngiven the interest, I productized my video hub! - have 1 place for video drafts + X, Youtube, tiktok vids - use the studio to comment + collab with others - get transcripts + add API keys for autosyncs/agent chat made with codex 5.3 🖤 linked below\n\n@EstePrimeWorld\n\nThis month was the first time I paid for an AI subscription other than Copilot, although I had occasionally used OpenCode with API keys in the past. I chose Codex, and honestly, it has made me much more productive. It is also genuinely fun to build new features and MVPs with it.\n\nImage: Codex desktop app showing its project selection screen.\n\nJul 26, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### DHH\n\n@dhh\n\nFor complicated agent work, it's amazing how much GPT5.5 has improved. I found 5.2 to be very far behind Opus. Now using Opus 4.7 after 5.5 feels like a big step backwards. Gotta love this level of competion! Strong comeback for OpenAI.\n\nMay 22, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Bindu Reddy\n\n@bindureddy\n\nFinally moved 90% of our hard coding workloads over to Codex For some reason Opus seemed to have gotten less performant over time 🤷‍♀️ It’s also refusing more requests Looking forward to even more capable and efficient Codex\n\nApr 11, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### David Marcus\n\n@davidmarcus\n\nIt's wild that every time you run a Codex code review from Claude Code, it finds critical issues. Not 95% of the times, 100%.\n\nMar 28, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### Victor Mota\n\n@vimota\n\nOpenAI got me with the 2x increased usage limits on the Codex desktop app. It's a really nice experience. Super smooth - claude code app is so laggy. And the handoff experience is amazing. > I started a session locally on codex app > had to leave so I handed it off to codex cloud (with 2 attempts) > got back to my computer, compared both attempts, picked the better one, synced it back to my computer > continued to iterate on it locally\n\nMar 13, 2026\n\nImage\n\n### ashe\n\n@ashebytes\n\ngiven the interest, I productized my video hub! - have 1 place for video drafts + X, Youtube, tiktok vids - use the studio to comment + collab with others - get transcripts + add API keys for autosyncs/agent chat made with codex 5.3 🖤 linked below\n\nMar 5, 2026\n\nImage\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCreate ChatKit session | OpenAI API Reference (https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/typescript/resources/beta/subresources/chatkit/subresources/sessions/methods/create)\nciteturn28sear